1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,675
Most smart home hubs are just lifeless black cylinders with zero personality.

2
00:00:04,675 --> 00:00:09,814
For Hack Club's Half Life, I wanted to build something with actual life and presence.

3
00:00:09,814 --> 00:00:14,780
Meet Hux, a desktop AI smart home companion inspired by Jarvis.

4
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:23,472
At its center is a color IPS display showing expressive animated eye emotions, encircled by an Arc-Reactor RGB status halo.

5
00:00:23,472 --> 00:00:33,692
Powered by an ESP32-S3, it controls Home Assistant locally over Wi-Fi with zero cloud lag, paired with an I2S digital mic and speaker.

6
00:00:33,692 --> 00:00:36,770
And it's all designed under a sixty-five dollar budget.

7
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:40,474
Now, let me walk you through the basics of how this comes together!

